{"title": "Sectional Mock #61 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The given histogram represents the marks of students in Mathematics test of a certain class. The total number of students is 350.</p><p>Study the graph and answer the question that follows.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 48\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19955/image061.png\"></p><p>What is the ratio of the total number of students who scored 140 marks and above to the total number of students who scored marks between 60 to 120?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2339;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 350 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 48\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19955/image061.png\"></p><p>140 &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 60 &#2360;&#2375; 120 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["110 : 137", "9 :11", "11 : 9", "137 : 110"], "options_hi": ["110 : 137", "9 :11", "11 : 9", "137 : 110"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of students who scored 140 marks and above = 55 + 40 + 15 = 110</p><p>Total number of students who scored marks between 60 to 120 = 32 + 45 + 60 = 137</p><p>Required ratio = 110: 137</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of students who scored 140 marks and above = 55 + 40 + 15 = 110</p><p>Total number of students who scored marks between 60 to 120 = 32 + 45 + 60 = 137</p><p>Required ratio = 110: 137</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A retailer purchased a batch of goods for Rs. 7500. Due to a manufacturing defect, 10% of the goods were damaged. If the retailer wants to make a profit of 30% on the remaining goods, at what price should the undamaged goods be sold?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; 7500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2376;&#2330; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;&#2339; &#2342;&#2379;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339;, 10% &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2340;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; 30% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2340;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 9750", "Rs. 8025", "Rs. 9000", "Rs. 8775"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 9750", "&#2352;&#2369;. 8025", "&#2352;&#2369;. 9000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 8775"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>C.P of undamaged goods = 7500 * 90/100 = Rs. 6750</p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 6750 * 130/100 </p><p>= Rs. 8775</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P of undamaged goods = 7500 * 90/100 = Rs. 6750</p><p>Hence, the required S.P = 6750 * 130/100 </p><p>= Rs. 8775</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X = 11 + (11/2) + (11/4) + (11/8) + (11/16) + ......&#8734;, then find the value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = 11 + (11/2) + (11/4) + (11/8) + (11/16) + ......&#8734;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["11", "2", "22", "121"], "options_hi": ["11", "2", "22", "121"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=205 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=179 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=507 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image005.png\"></p><p>Sum = a/ (1  -  r)</p><p><img width=95 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=205 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=179 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=507 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image005.png\"></p><p>Sum = a/ (1  -  r)</p><p><img width=95 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27449/image008.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Evaluate:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3cos<sup>3</sup>&#952; - 2cos&#952;", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3cos<sup>3</sup>&#952; - 2cos&#952;", "options_en": ["tan&#952;", "cot<sup>2</sup>&#952;", "cot&#952;", "tan<sup>2</sup>&#952;"], "options_hi": ["&#2340;&#2344;&#952;", "&#2326;&#2366;&#2335;<sup>2</sup>&#952;", "&#2326;&#2366;&#2335;&#952;", "&#2340;&#2344;<sup>2</sup>&#952;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Numerator: 3cos&ge;&#952; - 2cos&#952; = cos&#952; (3cos&#178;&#952; - 2) </p><p>Denominator: sin&#952; - 3sin&ge;&#952; = sin&#952; (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;) </p><p>Fraction = [cos&#952; (3cos&#178;&#952; - 2)] / [sin&#952; (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)] </p><p>= cot&#952; [(3cos&#178;&#952; - 2) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)] </p><p>= cot&#952; [(3(1 - sin&#178;&#952;) - 2) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)] </p><p>= cot&#952; [(3 - 3sin&#178;&#952; - 2) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)]</p><p>= cot&#952; [(1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)]</p><p>= cot&#952; </p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Numerator: 3cos&ge;&#952; - 2cos&#952; = cos&#952; (3cos&#178;&#952; - 2) </p><p>Denominator: sin&#952; - 3sin&ge;&#952; = sin&#952; (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;) </p><p>Fraction = [cos&#952; (3cos&#178;&#952; - 2)] / [sin&#952; (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)] </p><p>= cot&#952; [(3cos&#178;&#952; - 2) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)] </p><p>= cot&#952; [(3(1 - sin&#178;&#952;) - 2) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)] </p><p>= cot&#952; [(3 - 3sin&#178;&#952; - 2) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)]</p><p>= cot&#952; [(1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;) / (1 - 3sin&#178;&#952;)]</p><p>= cot&#952; </p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following statement(s) is/are true?</p><p>I. <img width=112 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image006.png\"></p><p>II. <img width=120 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image007.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;/&#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p><p>I. <img width=112 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image006.png\"></p><p>II. <img width=120 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image007.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["Both I and II", "Only I", "Neither I nor II", "Only II"], "options_hi": ["I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I", "&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><b>From I:</b> <img width=101 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image008.png\"></p><p>Taking square of all the terms, we get</p><p><img width=169 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image010.png\"></p><p>By taking LCM, we get</p><p><img width=120 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image011.png\">(which is not possible)</p><p>Hence, this statement is false.</p><p><b>From II:</b> <img width=120 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image007.png\"></p><p>Taking square of all the terms, we get</p><p><img width=177 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=78 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image013.png\"></p><p>By taking LCM, we get</p><p><img width=119 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image014.png\">(which is correct)</p><p>Hence, this statement is true.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>From I:</b> <img width=101 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image008.png\"></p><p>Taking square of all the terms, we get</p><p><img width=169 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image009.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image010.png\"></p><p>By taking LCM, we get</p><p><img width=120 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image011.png\">(which is not possible)</p><p>Hence, this statement is false.</p><p><b>From II:</b> <img width=120 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image007.png\"></p><p>Taking square of all the terms, we get</p><p><img width=177 height=47 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=78 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image013.png\"></p><p>By taking LCM, we get</p><p><img width=119 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image014.png\">(which is correct)</p><p>Hence, this statement is true.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sum of the two numbers P and Q is 146. If the sum of 8 times the value of P and 3 times the value of Q is 838, find the value of Q.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 146 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; P &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; 8 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; 3 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 838 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["66", "72", "78", "60"], "options_hi": ["66", "72", "78", "60"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>P + Q = 146 ...........(i)</p><p>8P + 3Q = 838 .........(ii)</p><p>Eq(ii)  -  3 * eq(i), we get -</p><p>8P + 3Q  -  3P  -  3Q = 838  -  3 * 146</p><p>5 P = 838  -  438</p><p>5 P = 400</p><p>P = 80</p><p>Q = 146  -  80 = 66</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P + Q = 146 ...........(i)</p><p>8P + 3Q = 838 .........(ii)</p><p>Eq(ii)  -  3 * eq(i), we get -</p><p>8P + 3Q  -  3P  -  3Q = 838  -  3 * 146</p><p>5 P = 838  -  438</p><p>5 P = 400</p><p>P = 80</p><p>Q = 146  -  80 = 66</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the ratio of two numbers is 3: 1 and their LCM is 126, then the sum of the two numbers is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:1 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; 126 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["172", "168", "196", "184"], "options_hi": ["172", "168", "196", "184"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers are 3X and X.</p><p>LCM of 3X and X = 3X</p><p>Given,</p><p>3X = 126</p><p>X = 42</p><p>Sum of numbers = 3X + X = 4X = 4 * 42 = 168</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers are 3X and X.</p><p>LCM of 3X and X = 3X</p><p>Given,</p><p>3X = 126</p><p>X = 42</p><p>Sum of numbers = 3X + X = 4X = 4 * 42 = 168</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of a rectangular field is 396 m&#178;, whose sides are in the ratio of 11:9. What is the perimeter of the rectangular field?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 396 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 11:9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["76 m", "80 m", "78 m", "74 m"], "options_hi": ["76 &#2350;&#2368;", "80 &#2350;&#2368;", "78 &#2350;&#2368;", "74 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let sides be 11k and 9k.</p><p>Area = 11k  X  9k = 99k&#178; = 396,</p><p>so k&#178; = 4,</p><p>k = 2.</p><p>Sides = 22 m and 18 m.</p><p>Perimeter = 2(22 + 18) = <b>80 m</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let sides be 11k and 9k.</p><p>Area = 11k  X  9k = 99k&#178; = 396,</p><p>so k&#178; = 4,</p><p>k = 2.</p><p>Sides = 22 m and 18 m.</p><p>Perimeter = 2(22 + 18) = <b>80 m</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pranav borrows a sum of &#8377;598397at the rate of 20% per annum simple interest. At the end of the first year, he repays &#8377;24284 towards return of principal amount borrowed. If Pranav clears all pending dues at the end of the second year, including interest payment that accrued during the first year, how much does he pay (in &#8377;) at the end of the second year?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2357; 20% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#8377;598397 &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#8377;24284 &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2357; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2367;&#2340; &#2348;&#2325;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2368; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["812514", "808615", "818513", "817567"], "options_hi": ["812514", "808615", "818513", "817567"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Interest for 1<sup>st</sup> year = (598,397  X  20  X  1)/100 = &#8377;119,679.40</p><p>Total amount after 1 year = &#8377;598,397 + &#8377;119,679.40 = &#8377;718,076.40</p><p>Remaining principal at the end of the first year is after repayment = &#8377;598,397 - &#8377;24,284 = &#8377;574,113</p><p>Interest for the second year on the remaining principal = (&#8377;574,113  X  20  X  1) / 100 = &#8377;114,822.60</p><p>Total amount due at the end of second year = &#8377;574,113 + &#8377;114,822.60 + &#8377;119,679.40 = &#8377;808,615</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Interest for 1<sup>st</sup> year = (598,397  X  20  X  1)/100 = &#8377;119,679.40</p><p>Total amount after 1 year = &#8377;598,397 + &#8377;119,679.40 = &#8377;718,076.40</p><p>Remaining principal at the end of the first year is after repayment = &#8377;598,397 - &#8377;24,284 = &#8377;574,113</p><p>Interest for the second year on the remaining principal = (&#8377;574,113  X  20  X  1) / 100 = &#8377;114,822.60</p><p>Total amount due at the end of second year = &#8377;574,113 + &#8377;114,822.60 + &#8377;119,679.40 = &#8377;808,615</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The curved surface area of the sphere is 154 cm<sup>2</sup>. Find the volume of the sphere (rounded off to one digit after decimal) .</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 154 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2340;&#2325;)&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["156.9 cm<sup>3</sup>", "179.7 cm<sup>3</sup>", "161.1 cm<sup>3</sup>", "147.8 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["156.9 cm<sup>3</sup>", "179.7 cm<sup>3</sup>", "161.1 cm<sup>3</sup>", "147.8 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Curved surface area of the sphere is 154 <img width=29 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image025.png\"></p><p>4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 154</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=55 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image026.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=24 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image027.png\"></p><p>r = <img width=15 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image028.png\">cm</p><p>Volume of the sphere =<img width=16 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image029.png\">&#960;r<sup>3</sup></p><p>= <img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image030.png\"></p><p>= 179.7 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Curved surface area of the sphere is 154 <img width=29 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image025.png\"></p><p>4&#960;r<sup>2</sup> = 154</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=55 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image026.png\"></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = <img width=24 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image027.png\"></p><p>r = <img width=15 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image028.png\">cm</p><p>Volume of the sphere =<img width=16 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image029.png\">&#960;r<sup>3</sup></p><p>= <img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20888/image030.png\"></p><p>= 179.7 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two similar pieces of an item were purchased by paying the same amount for each, and they were sold, respectively, for a profit of 25% and a loss of 20%. What was his profit percentage?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2368;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 25% &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2324;&#2352; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2342;&#2375;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "4.5", "2.5", "5"], "options_hi": ["2", "4.5", "2.5", "5"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price = p + p = 2p</p><p>Selling price = 1.25p + 0.8p = 2.05p</p><p>Profit percentage = [(2.05p  -  2p)/2p]*100 = 2.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price = p + p = 2p</p><p>Selling price = 1.25p + 0.8p = 2.05p</p><p>Profit percentage = [(2.05p  -  2p)/2p]*100 = 2.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat can cover 3K km in upstream in 9 hours. If the ratio of the speed of the boat in still water and speed of the stream is 7: 2, then in how much time it will cover K km in downstream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 3K &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7:2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; K &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["2(1/3) hours", "2(1/2) hours", "2 hours", "1(2/3) hours"], "options_hi": ["2(1/3) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "2(1/2) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "1(2/3) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of the boat in still water and speed of the stream are 7x km/h and 2x km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 3K/9 = K/3</p><p>=&gt; K/3 = 7x  -  2x</p><p>=&gt; K = 5x * 3 = 15x</p><p>So, required time = 15x/(7x + 2x) = 15/9 = 1(2/3) hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of the boat in still water and speed of the stream are 7x km/h and 2x km/h</p><p>Upstream speed = 3K/9 = K/3</p><p>=&gt; K/3 = 7x  -  2x</p><p>=&gt; K = 5x * 3 = 15x</p><p>So, required time = 15x/(7x + 2x) = 15/9 = 1(2/3) hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the LCM of U and 12 is 156 and the HCF of U and 15 is 1, find the sum of the digits of U.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; U &#2324;&#2352; 12 &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) 156 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; U &#2324;&#2352; 15 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) 1 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; U &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "3", "2", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "3", "2", "4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>LCM of U and 12 is 156 and the HCF of U and 15 is 1</p><p>So, U = 13</p><p>sum of the digits of U = 1 + 3 = 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>LCM of U and 12 is 156 and the HCF of U and 15 is 1</p><p>So, U = 13</p><p>sum of the digits of U = 1 + 3 = 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A solid cone of height 21 m and radius of base 28 m is melted to form a solid cylinder of radius 14 m and height 10 m. How much material is wasted in this process?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>21 m &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; 28 m &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 14 m &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 10 m &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12286 m<sup>3</sup>", "11088 m<sup>3</sup>", "12340 m<sup>3</sup>", "11240 m<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["12286 m<sup>3</sup>", "11088 m<sup>3</sup>", "12340 m<sup>3</sup>", "11240 m<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>The volume of the cone = 1/3 * &#8719; * r<sup>2</sup> * h = 1/3 * 22/7 * 28 * 28 * 21 </p><p>= 17248 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>The volume of the cylinder = &#8719; * r<sup>2</sup> * h = 22/7 * 14 * 14 * 10 = 6160 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>The value = 17248  -  6160 = 11088 m<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The volume of the cone = 1/3 * &#8719; * r<sup>2</sup> * h = 1/3 * 22/7 * 28 * 28 * 21 </p><p>= 17248 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>The volume of the cylinder = &#8719; * r<sup>2</sup> * h = 22/7 * 14 * 14 * 10 = 6160 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>The value = 17248  -  6160 = 11088 m<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x<sup>2</sup> + 49 - 16x = 0, then (x - 4)<sup>3</sup>  -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x<sup>2</sup> + 49 - 16x = 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (x - 4)<sup>3</sup>  -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["60&radic;60", "63&radic;60", "61&radic;60", "57&radic;60"], "options_hi": ["60 <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006061.png\">", "63 <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006061.png\">", "61 <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006061.png\">", "57 <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-006061.png\">"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/9987123.png\"><br></p><p><br></p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/9987123.png\"><br></p><p><br></p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The sides of a triangle are 12, 14, and 9. The radius of a circle is equal to the perimeter of this triangle. Find the circumference of this circle.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 12, 14 &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["110 cm", "220 cm", "180 cm", "260 cm"], "options_hi": ["110 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "220 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "180 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "260 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Perimeter = 12 + 14 + 9 = 35 cm</p><p>Radius of circle = 35 cm</p><p>Circumference of circle = 2 &#960; r = 2 x (22/7) x 35 = 220 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Perimeter = 12 + 14 + 9 = 35 cm</p><p>Radius of circle = 35 cm</p><p>Circumference of circle = 2 &#960; r = 2 x (22/7) x 35 = 220 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A is chasing B in the same interval of time. A Jumps 8 times, while B Jumps 6 times. But the distance covered by A in 7 jumps is the same as that of B in 5 jumps. The ratio between the speeds of A and B is.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A 8 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; B 6 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 7 &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368;, B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 5 &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["32 : 24", "30 : 56", "20 : 21", "28 : 36"], "options_hi": ["32 : 24", "30 : 56", "20 : 21", "28 : 36"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>7 jumps of A = 5 jumps of B</p><p>A = <img width=23 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image056.png\"></p><p>8 jumps of A =<img width=32 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image057.png\"></p><p>Ratio between the speeds of A and B = <img width=72 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image058.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>7 jumps of A = 5 jumps of B</p><p>A = <img width=23 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image056.png\"></p><p>8 jumps of A =<img width=32 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image057.png\"></p><p>Ratio between the speeds of A and B = <img width=72 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image058.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following pie charts show the result of a survey. A survey conducted on 3000 people staying in various societies and having various favourite movies.</p><p><img width=325 height=336 id=\"Chart 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19504/image005.png\"> <img width=402 height=336 id=\"Chart 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19504/image006.png\"></p><p>If the favourite movie of 40% people of society Q is D, then what will be the ratio of people who like movie D except society Q to total number of people staying in society S?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2360;&#2379;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2361;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; 3000 &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2344; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366; &#2347;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"325\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19504/image005.png\"> <img width=\"402\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19504/image006.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2379;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2368; Q &#2325;&#2375; 40% &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366; &#2347;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2350; D &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2379;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2368; Q &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2354;&#2381;&#2350; D &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2379;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2368; S &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2361;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["8: 21", "9: 25", "4: 15", "9: 22"], "options_hi": ["8: 21", "9: 25", "4: 15", "9: 22"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Number of people who like movie D in society Q = 3000 * (120/360) * (40/100) = 400</p><p>Total number of people who like movie D = 3000 * 20/100 = 600</p><p>Number of people except society Q like movie D = 600  -  400 = 200</p><p>Total number of people staying in society S = 3000 * 90/360 = 750</p><p>Required ratio = 200: 750 = 4: 15 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of people who like movie D in society Q = 3000 * (120/360) * (40/100) = 400</p><p>Total number of people who like movie D = 3000 * 20/100 = 600</p><p>Number of people except society Q like movie D = 600  -  400 = 200</p><p>Total number of people staying in society S = 3000 * 90/360 = 750</p><p>Required ratio = 200: 750 = 4: 15 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum amounts to Rs.4298.4 at 13.2% rate of simple interest after 7.5 years. What is the simple interest on same sum at 6.5 rate of interest after 2 years and 6 months?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>7.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; 13.2% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2352;&#2369;. 4298.4 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2343;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 6.5 &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.351", "Rs.297", "Rs.339", "Rs.373"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 351", "&#2352;&#2369;. 297", "&#2352;&#2369;. 339", "&#2352;&#2369;. 373"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let sum = Rs. P</p><p>Then, 4298.4  -  P = P * 13.2 * 7.5/100</p><p>P = 2160</p><p>New time period = 2 + 6/12 = 5/2 years</p><p>Now, SI on same sum at 6.5 rate of interest after 2 years and 6 months</p><p>= 2160 * 6.5 * (5/2))/100</p><p>= <b>Rs.351</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let sum = Rs. P</p><p>Then, 4298.4  -  P = P * 13.2 * 7.5/100</p><p>P = 2160</p><p>New time period = 2 + 6/12 = 5/2 years</p><p>Now, SI on same sum at 6.5 rate of interest after 2 years and 6 months</p><p>= 2160 * 6.5 * (5/2))/100</p><p>= <b>Rs.351</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x  -  2/x = 5, x &#8800; 0, then what is the value of (x<sup>4</sup>  -  8/x<sup>2</sup>)/(x<sup>2</sup>  -  4x  -  2)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x - 2/x = 5, x &#8800; 0, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sup>4</sup> - 8/x<sup>2</sup>)/(x<sup>2</sup> - 4x - 2) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["125", "145", "155", "135"], "options_hi": ["125", "145", "155", "135"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>x  -  2/x = 5</p><p>(x<sup>4</sup>  -  8/x<sup>2</sup>)/(x<sup>2</sup>  -  4x  -  2)</p><p>Divide by x into numerator and denominator - </p><p>= (x<sup>3</sup>  -  8/x<sup>3</sup>)/(x  -  4  -  2/x) </p><p>= (x  -  2/x)(x<sup>2</sup> + 4/x<sup>2</sup> + x*2/x)/(5  -  4)</p><p>= 5[(x - 2/x)<sup>2</sup> + 2*x*2/x + 2]</p><p>= 5(5<sup>2</sup> + 4 + 2)</p><p>= 155</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x  -  2/x = 5</p><p>(x<sup>4</sup>  -  8/x<sup>2</sup>)/(x<sup>2</sup>  -  4x  -  2)</p><p>Divide by x into numerator and denominator - </p><p>= (x<sup>3</sup>  -  8/x<sup>3</sup>)/(x  -  4  -  2/x) </p><p>= (x  -  2/x)(x<sup>2</sup> + 4/x<sup>2</sup> + x*2/x)/(5  -  4)</p><p>= 5[(x - 2/x)<sup>2</sup> + 2*x*2/x + 2]</p><p>= 5(5<sup>2</sup> + 4 + 2)</p><p>= 155</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The simplified value of <img width=192 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image017.png\"> is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p><img width=192 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image017.png\"> &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["527", "425", "493", "391"], "options_hi": ["527", "425", "493", "391"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=192 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image017.png\"></p><p><img width=144 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image018.png\"></p><p><img width=124 height=53 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image019.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image020.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=43 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image022.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=192 height=57 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image017.png\"></p><p><img width=144 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image018.png\"></p><p><img width=124 height=53 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image019.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=55 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image020.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=43 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image022.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Pipe A can fill a tank in 8 hours, and Pipe B can fill the same tank in 12 hours. They work together for 3 hours, after which a leak (which empties the tank in 24 hours) opens. How much longer will it take to fill the tank completely?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; 3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2367;&#2360;&#2366;&#2357; &#2326;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; (&#2332;&#2379; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 24 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;)&#2404; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["5 h", "5 h 15 m", "5 h 30 m", "6 h"], "options_hi": ["5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>A+B rate = 1/8 + 1/12 = 5/24 tank/hr =&gt; in 3 h = 15/24 = 5/8 done</p><p>Remaining = 3/8; leak rate = 1/24 =&gt; net = 1/8 + 1/12  -  1/24 = 1/6 tank/hr</p><p>Time = (3/8)/(1/6) = 2.25 h = 2 h 15 m =&gt; total = 3 h + 2 h 15 m = 5 h 15 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A+B rate = 1/8 + 1/12 = 5/24 tank/hr =&gt; in 3 h = 15/24 = 5/8 done</p><p>Remaining = 3/8; leak rate = 1/24 =&gt; net = 1/8 + 1/12  -  1/24 = 1/6 tank/hr</p><p>Time = (3/8)/(1/6) = 2.25 h = 2 h 15 m =&gt; total = 3 h + 2 h 15 m = 5 h 15 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>The given expression is equal to: (cotB  -  tanB).sinB.cosB.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>(cotB - tanB).sinB.cosB</p>", "options_en": ["1  -  2sec<sup>2</sup>B", "1  -  2cos<sup>2</sup>B", "2cos<sup>2</sup>B - 1", "2sec<sup>2</sup>B - 1"], "options_hi": ["1 - 2sec<sup>2</sup>B", "1 - 2cos<sup>2</sup>B", "2cos<sup>2</sup>B - 1", "2sec<sup>2</sup>B - 1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>(cotB  -  tanB).sinB.cosB</p><p>= (cosB/sinB  -  sinB/cosB).sinB.cosB</p><p>= [(cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  sin<sup>2</sup>B)/sinB.cosB].sinB.cosB</p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  sin<sup>2</sup>B)</p><p>= cos2B</p><p>= 1  -  2sin<sup>2</sup>B or 2cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(cotB  -  tanB).sinB.cosB</p><p>= (cosB/sinB  -  sinB/cosB).sinB.cosB</p><p>= [(cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  sin<sup>2</sup>B)/sinB.cosB].sinB.cosB</p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  sin<sup>2</sup>B)</p><p>= cos2B</p><p>= 1  -  2sin<sup>2</sup>B or 2cos<sup>2</sup>B  -  1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many times digit '6' appears in numbers which are perfect square from 2 to 300?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2 &#2360;&#2375; 300 &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; '6' &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366;&#2312; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["10", "9", "7", "6"], "options_hi": ["10", "9", "7", "6"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Perfect squares from 2 to 300 in which 6 appears are:</p><p>16, 36, 64, 169, 196, 256</p><p>Hence, 6 appears 6 times in perfect squares from 2 to 300.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Perfect squares from 2 to 300 in which 6 appears are:</p><p>16, 36, 64, 169, 196, 256</p><p>Hence, 6 appears 6 times in perfect squares from 2 to 300.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The age of Kiran after three years is 42 years. If the ratio of present age of Kiran and Shubham is 13:11 respectively, then find the present age of Shubham.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; 42 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2369;&#2349;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 13:11 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2369;&#2349;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["22 years", "44 years", "33 years", "55 years"], "options_hi": ["22 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "44 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "33 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "55 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Present age of Kiran = 42  -  3 = 39 years</p><p>Present age of Shubham = 39*11/13 = 33 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Present age of Kiran = 42  -  3 = 39 years</p><p>Present age of Shubham = 39*11/13 = 33 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}]}